<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stuart Restoration</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1660</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Restoration of 1660, English Restoration</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Stuart Restoration was the return of the monarchy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and Ireland in 1660, when Charles II came back from exile after the collapse of the Commonwealth and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a>. In Scotland it revived the separate parliament, Privy Council and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>, leading to conflict with the Presbyterian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/covenanters">Covenanters</a>. The term also names the period of Charles II's reign, known for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> and science.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stuart-restoration.jpg" alt="Stuart Restoration" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Michael Wright · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_II_of_England_in_Coronation_robes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
